<title>UK: News Corp plans $800 mln of disposals - paper.</title>
<headline>News Corp plans $800 mln of disposals - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>News Corporation, the media empire led by mogul Rupert Murdoch, plans to sell $800 million of assets to fund its global satellite television expansion while retaining investment grade status for its securities, said the Financial Times on Thursday.</p>
<p>The sale will involve undefined non-core assets, said the report which added that the stake in Australia's Ansett Airlines and publisher Harper Collins would not be in the firing line. --London newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
